WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:16.460
Spider Monkey Island was covered in clouds of dust and dirt.

2
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.881
There was a loud hissing noise and eagle feathers everywhere.

3
00:00:21.882 --> 00:00:25.423
Everyone's feet and hands hurt from drumming and stamping their feet.

4
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:29.404
Dr. Dolittle and Long Arrow looked over the cliff.

5
00:00:30.248 --> 00:00:33.489
The hanging stone had fallen exactly into the hole.

6
00:00:33.509 --> 00:00:36.270
"We did it, my friend!"

7
00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.551
shouted the doctor in a hoarse voice.

8
00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:42.812
"That hissing noise is the air rushing out of the hole.

9
00:00:43.652 --> 00:00:45.593
The hollow is filling with water."

10
00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:48.854
They stood up and shook each other's hands.

11
00:00:49.794 --> 00:00:51.734
The island was no longer floating.

12
00:00:53.455 --> 00:00:56.876
One by one the people of Popsipetal came before the doctor.

13
00:00:57.756 --> 00:01:01.037
Each of them bowed and then placed their right hand on his shoulder.

14
00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:04.698
Dr. Dolittle did not understand what they were doing.

15
00:01:05.418 --> 00:01:08.379
Finally the chief's eldest son, the one Dr.

16
00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:11.240
Dolittle and Long Arrow had saved, came up to him.

17
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.382
He wore a long robe with a red sash across his right shoulder.

18
00:01:17.122 --> 00:01:19.843
He carried a large wreath made of eagle feathers.

19
00:01:20.663 --> 00:01:23.304
He removed the sash and placed it on Dr.

20
00:01:23.344 --> 00:01:24.164
Dolittle's shoulder.

21
00:01:25.196 --> 00:01:26.657
"What is the meaning of this?"

22
00:01:26.997 --> 00:01:27.858
the doctor cried.

23
00:01:29.178 --> 00:01:31.500
Long Arrow translated for the chief's son.

24
00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.761
"A chief may care deeply about his people.

25
00:01:35.582 --> 00:01:38.243
A chief may be brave enough to do foolish things.

26
00:01:39.204 --> 00:01:42.526
A chief may have great talents, like speaking to animals.

27
00:01:43.326 --> 00:01:46.148
But a king is a man who has all of these things.

28
00:01:47.028 --> 00:01:48.309
Hail King Jong!"

29
00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:52.191
"But who is this King Jong?"

30
00:01:52.551 --> 00:01:53.272
asked the doctor.

31
00:01:54.136 --> 00:01:55.817
"You are," answered Long Arrow.

32
00:01:56.558 --> 00:02:01.001
With that, the chief's son placed the crown of eagle feathers on the doctor's head.

33
00:02:01.862 --> 00:02:06.826
All the people began bowing and chanting "Zanming Jong!

34
00:02:07.366 --> 00:02:08.807
Zanming Jong!"

35
00:02:09.608 --> 00:02:12.070
This meant, "Long live King Jong."

36
00:02:13.131 --> 00:02:14.732
So on that day, Dr.

37
00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:17.194
Dolittle became the king of Popsipetal.

38
00:02:17.974 --> 00:02:19.936
But he was not a very happy king.

39
00:02:20.824 --> 00:02:24.006
King Jong was not allowed to go anywhere by himself.

40
00:02:24.926 --> 00:02:27.428
There were many duties for the king to carry out.

41
00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:31.350
Every day, the villagers came to the king with their problems.

42
00:02:32.411 --> 00:02:34.171
Long Arrow translated for them.

43
00:02:34.192 --> 00:02:38.774
"This man wants permission to plant more vegetables," he explained.

44
00:02:38.794 --> 00:02:41.976
"Oh, who cares," murmured the king.

45
00:02:41.996 --> 00:02:44.237
"Let him do whatever he wants."

46
00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:49.180
Every day, King Jong had lessons in the Popsipetal language.

47
00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:53.141
Learning animal languages was quite easy and fun.

48
00:02:53.942 --> 00:02:57.443
But King Jong found human languages difficult and boring.

49
00:02:57.463 --> 00:03:02.185
"Lu, la, lick, lur," he repeated.

50
00:03:03.085 --> 00:03:04.626
The king was always busy.

51
00:03:05.106 --> 00:03:06.427
So Tommy missed Dr.

52
00:03:06.447 --> 00:03:07.627
Dolittle very much.

53
00:03:07.647 --> 00:03:09.908
"Are you sleeping, Tommy?"

54
00:03:10.108 --> 00:03:11.789
Polynesia whispered in the dark.

55
00:03:12.749 --> 00:03:13.889
"No," he answered.

56
00:03:13.909 --> 00:03:17.751
"Tommy, we must get the doctor out of here," she said.

57
00:03:17.771 --> 00:03:19.892
"He's so miserable."

58
00:03:20.864 --> 00:03:22.004
"But what can we do?

59
00:03:22.444 --> 00:03:25.565
He always has those bodyguards around," Tommy said.

60
00:03:25.585 --> 00:03:27.786
"Tomorrow when Dr.

61
00:03:27.826 --> 00:03:32.447
Dolittle hears the people's problems, you will approach him," said Polynesia.

62
00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.128
"What should I say?"

63
00:03:34.448 --> 00:03:35.068
asked Tommy.

64
00:03:35.088 --> 00:03:37.109
"This is what you will say."

65
00:03:37.949 --> 00:03:40.109
She whispered something into Tommy's ear.

66
00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.551
The next day, King Jong sat on his throne again.

67
00:03:45.471 --> 00:03:48.772
How surprised and happy he was to see Tommy approach him.

68
00:03:49.716 --> 00:03:51.697
"Tommy!" he cried joyfully.

69
00:03:52.537 --> 00:03:55.679
Tommy bowed low and spoke in the dolphins' language.

70
00:03:56.599 --> 00:04:00.360
King Jong listened carefully and said, "I will be waiting."

71
00:04:01.781 --> 00:04:04.902
That evening, King Jong went to bed at the usual time.

72
00:04:05.843 --> 00:04:07.964
His bodyguards stood in front of the hut.

73
00:04:08.824 --> 00:04:12.545
They did not notice two spiders weaving a web above their heads.

74
00:04:13.546 --> 00:04:18.548
They also did not see the two small mice hiding in the trees with Polynesia.

75
00:04:19.836 --> 00:04:23.718
When she gave the signal, each mouse bit hard on the guards' toes.

76
00:04:24.499 --> 00:04:29.742
But before the guards could scream, the spiders swung their webs over their mouths and eyes.

77
00:04:30.882 --> 00:04:32.703
Polynesia flew inside the hut.

78
00:04:33.984 --> 00:04:36.506
Dr. Dolittle was dressed in his regular clothes.

79
00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:39.687
"We must hurry, Doctor," she whispered.

80
00:04:39.707 --> 00:04:41.628
"What about Tommy?

81
00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:43.549
Charles? Long Arrow?"

82
00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:44.410
he asked.

83
00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.672
"They'll meet us," Polynesia assured him.

84
00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:52.376
Together they ran out of the hut and disappeared into the woods.
